msgstr ""

#: includes/abilities/funnels/edit-flow.php:128
msgid "For \"duplicate\": choices the step type takes when duplicated, like {\"__duplicate_email\": true} to make a copy of a send_email step's email instead of sharing it."
msgstr ""

#: includes/abilities/funnels/edit-flow.php:134
msgid "For \"add\": the steps to add in order, the same step nodes groundhogg/create-flow takes, including branches."
msgstr ""

#: includes/abilities/funnels/edit-flow.php:142
msgid "For \"update\": only the settings to change, the rest are kept. Same shape as groundhogg/list-step-types describes. For if_else, include_condition replaces the include_filters groundhogg/get-flow returned, and exclude_condition the exclude_filters. A `branches` map (split_path, weighted_distribution) is merged branch by branch: give only the branches to change, the same condition/filters rule applies inside each, and null removes a branch (only if it has no steps)."
